# PSR-7e — RC evidence pack schema

## Intent

Close the **schema** half of PSR-7 R-EVIDENCE: a machine-readable release
candidate pack that binds **one git SHA** to security/release artifacts.

This wave lands schema + example + validator smoke only:

- No provenance attestation
- No staging deploy
- No claim that a real RC pack exists for tip

## Pack fields (summary)

| Field | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `git_sha` | Identical tip for all attached proofs |
| `collected_at` | ISO timestamp |
| `scorecard` | Path/digest of PSR-9 collector report |
| `secret_scan` | Tracked baseline result (+ optional history YES pack) |
| `sbom` | CycloneDX path + lockfile sha256 |
| `branch_protection` | print/verify artifact (live verify = YES) |
| `staging` | four-process / restore refs (live = YES) |
| `harbor` | tier + proof family statuses |
| `ops_identity` | shared_bearer vs session_jwt dual-accept status |
| `program_gates` | explicit booleans — must stay false until Architect |

## Validate

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-7e-rc-evidence-pack-smoke.mjs
```

## Next

`PSR-7f-branch-protection-print-ratchet` then fill a tip draft pack under
`reports/psr/` (gitignored) without claiming RC closed.
